<title>USA: U.S. DAP prices flat, ammonia slightly higher.</title>
<headline>U.S. DAP prices flat, ammonia slightly higher.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. cash diammonium phosphate prices were steady Friday and ammonia was slightly higher on good demand from southwestern farmers, cash sources said.</p>
<p>A week of relatively dry weather in Texas enabled the application of ammonia to cotton, milo and wheat crops, so that activity was supporting prices, dealers said.</p>
<p>			   Dlrs/short ton	Chg from Wednesday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla	   180-182			unc</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf     188-190			unc</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf	   228-230			up 3/flat</p>
<p>--(Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720)</p>
